{"step_index":711,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T01:40:04Z","content":"All three requested tasks have been completed strictly using verified data from the game build files and decompiled RAGE YSC scripts.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Deep Dispatcher Analysis Results (`analyze_dispatcher_deep.py`)\n\nInspecting the master narrative dispatcher `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs` (`Program_0E8E47D1`, directly imported by `story000.ysc.cs`) uncovered the concrete mission state management architecture:\n\n* **Mission Lookup Dispatcher (`func_109E09`)**:\n  * Evaluates **131 mission hashes** via a compiled binary search comparison tree (`as_i32(local_1) > 0x...` and `== 0x...`), verifying valid story mission IDs and updating stat telemetry.\n* **Chapter Transition Barrier Sweeper (`func_10AA55`)**:\n  * **Chapter 2 Barrier (`MTL_WAKE`)**: When advancing to Chapter 2, lines 572964–573008 execute a sweep that closes out and sets state flags for Chapter 1 side content:\n    * `FT_KMODSHP_SECOND`\n    * `COM_KBOS_SHOP`, `COM_KBOS_COLAT`, `COM_KBOS_RADR`, `COM_KBOS_NEIGHB`, `COM_KBOS_CLEAN`\n    * `HO_PAR_KEYCO`\n    * `RecoverDropTipShackDonnieAlive` / `RecoverDropTipShackDonnieDeadUnknown`\n  * **Chapter 4 Barrier (`MNY_HOTEL` / `MNY_HOTEL_AUTOLAUNCH`)**: Lines 572946–573082 resolve and sweep Chapter 3 asset flags:\n    * `ANT_SRCH` and `ANT_RECOV`\n    * `ANT_CHASE` / `ANT_CHASE_AUTOLAUNCH`\n    * `ANT_INTRO_APARTMENT` / `ANT_INTRO_STORAGE`\n* **Campaign Finale Win Condition (`func_10AD05`)**:\n  * Lines 573115–573127 contain the campaign completion condition:\n    ```csharp\n    if (Method_1(store, 0xF8FB7ACC /* BIL_FINALE_M */) != 0) return 1;\n    return Method_1(store, 0x96F9A142 /* BIL_FINAL_B */);\n    ```\n  * Evaluates `BIL_FINALE_M` (Ending M) OR `BIL_FINAL_B` (Ending B) as the valid campaign completion flags.\n\n---\n\n### 2. GXT2 Localization Table Scan Results\n\nA binary scan across all extracted RPF archives and raw payload chunks (over 75 GB of data) for the RAGE localization table magic `GXT2` / `2TXG` (`0x32545847` / `0x47585432`):\n\n* **Result**: **0 valid GXT2 text headers found** (verified by `work/gxt_scan.py` and `\n<truncated 550 bytes>\nject outputs have been updated with these verified facts:\n\n#### A. [`output/mission_order.json`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/mission_order.json)\n* Updated metadata with the GXT2 scan results and dispatcher evidence (`func_109E09`, `func_10AA55`, `func_10AD05`).\n* Assigned every mission a verified **`strand_type`** (`Main Story Core`, `Narrative Strand`, `Faction / Compound Strand`, `Tutorial Strand`, `Cutscene Checkpoint`, `Hangout Vignette`, etc.).\n* Flagged verified linear bottlenecks (`is_bottleneck`) and branching points (`branching`).\n\n#### B. [`output/mission_flow.mmd`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/mission_flow.mmd)\n* Visual Mermaid flowchart separating **Main Story Core** (blue) from **Side-Strands / Compounds** (gray).\n* Highlights **Linear Bottleneck Gates** (red: `INT_PROLO`, `INT_BANK`, `MTL_WAKE`, `BAN_FINAL`, `MNY_HOTEL`, `AIR_FINAL`, `BIL_PENT`, `FIN_CONT`, `INT_CRED`).\n* Renders parallel tracks within chapters and shows verified branching paths (orange: `BIL_PENT` Mendez vs. Brian, `AIR_FINAL` Data Hack Passed vs. Failed, `ROB_BOAT` Jason vs. Lucia).\n* Displays the 4 confirmed replay unlock links and the Chapter 1/3 barrier sweeps from `func_10AA55`.\n\n#### C. [`output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md)\n* Comprehensive speedrun technical reference detailing:\n  1. Full provenance and absence of unencrypted GXT2 text.\n  2. Main Story Core vs. Side-Strands prefix taxonomy.\n  3. Linear bottlenecks vs. parallel tracks.\n  4. Specific Any% speedrun skip opportunities (e.g., Chapter 1 compound skip potential verified by `MTL_WAKE` flag sweep).\n  5. Critical routing choices (`AIR_FINAL_DATA_HACK_FAILED` alarm skip potential, `BIL_MOTEL` combat vs. dialogue skip, `BIL_FINALE_M` vs. `BIL_FINAL_B` ending delta).\n\n*Copies of all three updated files have also been synced directly to [`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads).*","thinking":"The dispatcher analysis reveals that `func_109E09`, `func_10AA55`, and `func_10AD05` within the specified file are crucial for controlling game logic. Examination of the `mission_dependency_graph.json` also highlights how specific flags are set and cleared by different functions, for example, `MTL_WAKE` sweeps flags related to chapter 1 and `MNY_HOTEL` operates similarly for flags linked to chapter 3. Analyzing this flag manipulation is key to understanding win conditions.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
