{"step_index":724,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T01:47:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T20:47:09-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T20:47:09-05:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/<user>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c/gta6_mission_flow_chart.md`\nTotal Lines: 401\nTotal Bytes: 27080\nShowing lines 101 to 250\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 3. Chapter 2: Paradise Lost (Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)\n106: \n107: ### Mechanics & Structure\n108: - **Playable Character**: Heavily centered on **Lucia** during early recovery, then **permanently unlocks Dual Character Switching** via *\"Coffee Break\"*.\n109: - **Vehicle Fencing**: Unlocked via *\"Moses\"* (enabling Slim Jim vehicle thefts and custom garage registrations).\n110: - **Strict Chronological Sequence**: Unlike Chapter 3, Chapter 2 is organized into **4 sequential stages** that must be cleared in order (M23 through M44).\n111:   - **Stage 1: Motel Arrival & Medical (M23–M28)**: Infiltration, paying upkeep, Lucia solo medical run, and establishing fencing with Moses.\n112:   - **Stage 2: Debt Hustle & Gun Runs (M29–M37)**: Disguise setups, ambulance chasing, painkiller supply lines, and corner meetups.\n113:   - **Stage 3: Dual Character Switching & Robberies (M38–M40)**: *Coffee Break* unlocks instant partner switching; *Hit Avery Pawn* introduces business robberies.\n114:   - **Stage 4: Highway Escape & Move to Vice City (M41–M44)**: Vehicle recovery, Kelly County smugglers, and the motel evacuation climax in *Checking Out*.\n115: \n116: ```mermaid\n117: flowchart TD\n118:     C1_Trans[\"From Ch. 1: Doin' Gone\"] --> S1_Start\n119:     \n120:     subgraph S1[\"Stage 1: Motel Arrival & Fencing (M23 - M28)\"]\n121:         S1_Start[\"23. What's in the Bag?<br/>(Starlet Motel Arrival)\"] --> M24[\"24. Overnight Charges\"]\n122:         M24 --> M25[\"25. Take Care of Jason<br/>(Luc\n<truncated 5792 bytes>\nribution Bus\"| P63\n223:     M61 ==>|\"Top Distribution Bus\"| P64\n224:     \n225:     P68 & P69 & P67 --> M70[\"70. THE CARTEL HEIST<br/>★ MAJOR HEIST CLIMAX ★<br/>($10.5M Vault Raid Take)<br/>⚠️ KEEP $75k FOR CHAPTER 4 ABE GATE ⚠️\"]\n226:     \n227:     M70 -->|\"Hard Transition\"| C4_Start[\"→ Chapter 4: Ocean Beach Safehouse\"]\n228: ```\n229: \n230: ---\n231: \n232: ## 5. Chapter 4: Vice City Metro & Airport Takedown\n233: \n234: ### Mechanics & Structure\n235: - **Scope**: 25 main missions (M71 through M95).\n236: - **Safehouse**: Y Hotel (Ocean Beach headquarters).\n237: - **Mandatory Cash Gate (M75)**: In *Party Hard*, corrupt lawyer Abe Gonzalez demands a mandatory **$75,000 BuckMe wire transfer** to proceed.\n238: - **Strict Chronological Sequence**:\n239:   - **Stage 1: Beachhead & Abe Gate (M71–M75)**: Establishing Ocean Beach lifestyle and securing legal immunity.\n240:   - **Stage 2: Syndicate Operations (M76–M82)**: Harbor smuggling, blackmail photography, fitness front extortion, and body sanitization.\n241:   - **Stage 3: Dre'Quan Climax & Airport Recon (M83–M91)**: Celebrity protection, kidnapping, Dre'Quan concert finale (*Headliners*), and VCIA airport perimeter surveillance.\n242:   - **Stage 4: Airport Heist & Evacuation (M92–M95)**: Cargo infiltration (*Fully Catered*), the massive airport heist (*VCIA Takedown*), open-world lockdown (*Sunset*), and emergency evacuation (*Starting From Zero*).\n243: - **POINT OF NO RETURN**: *\"Sunset\"* permanently locks open-world activities and free roam saves, forcing continuous progression into Chapter 5.\n244: \n245: ```mermaid\n246: flowchart TD\n247:     C3_Trans[\"From Ch. 3: The Cartel Heist\"] --> S1_Start\n248:     \n249:     subgraph C4_S1[\"Stage 1: Beachhead & $75k Gate (M7